    "summary": "Man&#039;s horizontal loom (turkudi) made primarily of wood and comprising several elements including a breast beam (takala) and a beater made of strips of reed secured at top with two pieces of raffia palm fibre and covered at bottom with skin. A rocker bar (shuwaka) connects a pair of heddles. Curved wooden rods form the foot pedals (mataki). The warp threads are attached to a potsherd which acts as a drag weight (kunkuru).",
